| `canary.answer_sets.<name>.<question>` | object of copier answers | `default` gets `{}`; `skeleton` gets `frontend_stack` `none`, `showcase` `false` and `transports` `["grpc"]` | a set name of letters, digits, `.`, `_` or `-` mapped to answers to copier.yml questions, each within its choices and passing copier.yml's validators over its defaults | `scripts/canary.py`; `tests/integration/test_canary_wiring.py` | Adds, removes or changes a project the release canary renders; each set renders fresh and as an update from the previous release. Read only in the template repository: a generated project carries the block because its config loader declares the key, and absent, the canary writes `[using default] canary.answer_sets = {"default": {}, "skeleton": {"frontend_stack": "none", "showcase": false, "transports": ["grpc"]}}` to stderr. A set name that is not one plain segment, or answers that are not an object, are refused with exit 14. | the answers `make new` asks for: copier's own questions | always |
